content.text:
await page.setViewportSize({ width: 390, height: 844 });
```
ok

Landscape 8-lane 844x390: field fits, labels A S D F J K L ;, rings at 77% height (y≈308 of 390). Good. But pad sizes are huge in 844x390? Rings ~48px, pads ~48. Good.

Desktop 6-lane 1280x720: active lanes 1..6 with labels S D F J K L; hidden lane 0 at left x≈213 has a visible ghost ring with a big glow orb nearby (ghost effect); lane7 at right x≈1001 visible ghost/orange ring. Both hidden lanes show ghost rings due to ghost effects. The big white orb at x≈175,y≈200 and bright vertical beam is a lane-0 sweep. It looks like a comet, good. But the ghost lane ring at x≈213 is nearly as bright as active, and lane7's ring too. In the screenshot, timestamps 1:08 => DRIFT; the ghost events rhythmic at 65.3 etc. Both sides show ghost effects. It's clearly decorative because no key labels under them. Good.

But there's a concern: the "DRIFT" section HUD says 6 lanes, and visible ghost lanes on both edges. A player might tap them? No labels and dimmer. The sweep orb is very bright due to bloom, but it's a cool effect. Fine.

However, on desktop 6-lane, active lane1 (S) ring at x=300 and hidden lane0 at x≈213; gap 87px; pad zone for lane1 size clamp gap*1.02 → 89px; pad for lane0 hidden. Good. Rings mostly touch (active ring diameter ~100px, gap 130? Hmm).

Also the hit line spans all 8 lanes? In screenshot, hit line spans from x≈213 to x≈1001 (all lanes incl ghost) — looks like a full line. `hitLine.scale.x = v.spacing*(keyCount-1)+v.ring*1.5` = 2.16*5 + 1.95*1.5 = 10.8+2.925=13.7 world. Ghost lane positions are at (i-3.5)*2.16 = ±7.56, ±5.4; active edge lanes 1 and 6 at ±5.4. Hit line half-width 6.86 world, reaching just past lane1/6 but not to lane0/7 at ±7.56. Yet screenshot line appears to extend to ghost rings at ±7.56? Hmm, maybe because hit line sprite is centered at x=0 with scale 13.7; physically spans ±6.85. Ghost rings at x≈213 and 1001 are ±? Active rings at 300..866 (6), spacing ~113px, center 583. Hidden lane0 at 213 (87px left of S) = 2.16 world? Wait active lane1 at 300, lane0 at 213, difference 87 px; spacing 2.16 world ≈ 87 px; so lane0 = lane1 - 2.16. Active lane1 is -5.4 world, lane0 -7.56. Hit line spans ±6.85, so should end ~45px inside lane0 ring at 213 (ends at 213+45=258). Screenshot hit line seems to extend all the way to x=213? There is a horizontal line through ghost ring centers, yes. Maybe ghost ring's own line? The ring group's line is vertical only. Hmm could be the hitLine because scale 13.7 world at ~40px/world = 548px? Wait desktop px/world maybe 40; 13.7*40=548, spanning 1024? no. Let me not overanalyze; visually fine.

Now key issue: hidden lanes show ghost rings during flourish only. Good.

But I notice on desktop 6-lane that the lane 0 (ghost) ring is visible simultaneously with active lanes, and there's a big diamond note at x≈290, y≈285 (in lane1). The note travels down to ring at x=300,y≈544. Good.

Potential improvement: pad zones use `size = gap*1.02`, so for 6 lanes gap between active lane1 and lane2 ~113; pad size ~115px but ring diameter ~100; pad extends above/below ring. Fine.

Everything works. Need to test actual tapping and scoring. Use desktop 1280x720, start fresh, click a ring near a note? We can simulate keyboard presses at note times and check stats. E.g., chart notes at t≈3.535 lane 2. Start game and press D at ~3.5s. But timing manually tricky. Easier: use eval to call `pressLane(lane)` at exact appropriate times? We can detect nearest pending note and press with setTimeout. But the game has audio running; we can schedule eval:

```
const c=__cryout; const n=c.notes.find(n=>n.state==='pending'); const wait=(n.data.t-c.audio.time)*1000; setTimeout(()=>c.pressLane(n.lane), wait);
```
Then wait 1s and inspect stats. This uses pressLane directly and validates judgement. But the user-facing tap zone wiring (pointerdown) can be tested separately by clicking pad center when a note is due.

Let's test pointer tapping: restart game at 0 via clicking restart? Easiest reload page, click start, then evaluate to find next note and its pad position, then wait via setTimeout? We can't use setTimeout in Code Mode but shell sleep. In browser eval we can schedule a synthetic pointerdown at the pad right when note arrives:

```
() => {
 const c=window.__cryout;
 const n=c.notes.find(n=>n.state==='pending'&&n.data.t>c.audio.time+0.5);
 const pad=document.querySelector(`.pad[data-lane="${n.lane}"]`);
 const r=pad.getBoundingClientRect();
 const delay=(n.data.t-c.audio.time)*1000;
