Bug! Selecting cryout after quitting did not switch — track remains WORLD YEARNING. Why? `clickSel('.track-card[data-track="cryout"]')` — after quit, the start screen shows. The click handler:
```
for (const card of dom.trackCards) {
  card.addEventListener('click', () => {
    if (gameState !== 'boot' && gameState !== 'menu') return;
    if (card.dataset.track === selectedTrack.id) return;
    selectTrack(card.dataset.track);
  });
}
```
gameState is 'menu' after quit. Should work. But maybe the click didn't register because the card is outside the viewport or overlapped? On 1280x800, start screen might scroll (height content > 800), the track card might be visible. It clicked but maybe the overlay has scroll and element location is off? Our clickSel uses getBoundingClientRect center; should be fine.

Wait, after quitting, `dom.start.classList.add('show')` but maybe the result screen? Start shown true. The track-card might be under another overlay or have zero size? Let's check. Another possibility: the click at card center landed on a child `<span>` which bubbles to button — fine.

Wait, maybe the start overlay was still transitioning and `visibility` visible; fine.

Hmm, could the click have gone to another element because the card was below fold? At 1280x800, start screen uses start-grid two columns; content ~? Earlier at 1440x900 it fit. At 1280x800 likely fits. Let's debug by checking elementFromPoint at the card center and clicking again, reading state.

Also maybe `selectTrack` was called but immediately failed because `loadAudio` threw? No, then track would still be cryout. It remained world with label START SESSION, so selectTrack wasn't called at all.

Perhaps the overlay is not visible to pointer due to `dom.pause`? Quit closes pause. Start show.

Let's run a quick eval to click the card programmatically `.click()` and see if it switches. If programmatic works, the input click was intercepted. Let's check elementFromPoint.

